refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
intsapi_windows_cp_get stringkind""
Gets the current codepage.

&reftitle.parameters;
kind
The kind of operating system codepage to get, either 'ansi' or 'oem' (case-insensitive). Any other value refers to the current codepage of the process.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
If kind is 'ansi', the current ANSI code page of the operating system is returned. If kind is 'oem', the current OEM code page of the operating system is returned. Otherwise, the current codepage of the process is returned.
The current codepage of the process is the encoding PHP uses when converting strings such as paths, arguments, and environment variables. It is set at startup from the internal_encoding and default_charset INI settings (65001, UTF-8, by default), and is changed by sapi_windows_cp_set as well as by later changes to these INI settings, such as ini_set. It is not the codepage of the console.
